    "title": "Spurs vs. Clippers: How to watch the game, who's starting, who's out",
    "text": "Spurs (49-18) vs. Clippers (34-33) When/where: 9 p.m. Monday at Inuit Dome, Los Angeles TV/radio: KENS, Peacock/NBC SN; 1200 AM, 1350 AM (Spanish), 107.5 FM (Spanish). PROBABLE STARTERSSpurs: PG De'Aaron Fox (6-3, 9th year), SG Stephon Castle (6-6, 2nd); SF Devin Vassell (6-5, 6th), PF Julian Champagnie (6-7, 4th), C Victor Wembanyama (7-4, 3rd).  Clippers: PG Kris Dunn (6-3, 10th), SG Kobe Sanders (6-8, 1st), SF Kawhi Leonard (6-6, 14th), PF Derrick Jones Jr. (6-6, 10th), C Brook Lopez (7-1, 18th). RESERVESSpurs: G/F Keldon Johnson (6-6, 7th), C Luke Kornet (7-1, 9th), F Harrison Barnes (6-7, 14th), C Bismack Biyombo (6-8, 15th), G Lindy Waters III (6-5, 5th), C/F Kelly Olynyk (6-11, 13th) G Jordan McLaughlin (5-11, 7th) F Carter Bryant (6-6, 1st), C Mason Plumlee (7-0, 13th). Inactive: David Jones Garcia (two-way), Harrison Ingram (two-way), Emanuel Miller (two-way), Dylan Harper (right calf contusion). Clippers: F Nicolas Batum (6-7, 18th), G Bogdan Bogdanovic (6-5, 9th), G Cam Christie (6-5, 2nd), G Darius Garland  (6-1, 8th), F Isaiah Jackson (6-8, 5th), G/F Bennedict Mathurin (6-5, 4th), F Jordan Miller (6-5, 3rd), G TyTy Washington (6-3, 4th). Inactive: Sean Padulla (two-way), Norchad Omier (two-way), Yanic Konan Niederhauser (right foot injury), Bradley Beal (left hip fracture).   COACHESSpurs: Mitch Johnson.Clippers: Ty Lue. STAT LEADERSSpurs: Points, Wembanyama (24.3 per game). Rebounds, Wembanyama (11.2). Assists, Castle (7.0). Steals, Castle/Fox (1.2). Blocks, Wembanyama (2.9). Clippers: Points, Leonard (28.3 per game). Rebounds, Leonard (6.3). Assists, Garland (6.0), Steals, Leonard (2.0), Blocks, Jones/Lopez (1.1). NOTABLE• The Clippers are the first team in NBA history to move their record to better than .500 after being at many as 15 games below that mark in the same season. Los Angeles has won 28 of its past 40 contests after beginning the campaign 6-21. • Leonard suffered a left ankle sprain in the Clippers' loss against Sacramento on Saturday and is uncertain for Monday's game. The All-Star forward has topped 20 points in 45 consecutive games, breaking Bob McAdoo's franchise record set in 1974-75. • The Spurs have dropped five in a row on the road against the Clippers, and have never won at the Intuit Dome (0-2). Jeff McDonald",
